analysisWe need to produce assert statement for comment.

We need to parse: In add(int index, E obj) method. The comment:

// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the initial size of the list inclusive, then for every valid index from this index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null and the old element at this index is null, or the element at the next position equals the old element at this index.

Interpretation: Precondition: index between 0 and old size inclusive (i.e., old size before insertion). Then for every i in [index, oldSize-1] (valid old indices), after insertion, the element at position i+1 (next position) is either null and the old element at i was null, or element at i+1 equals old element at i.

We need to use this.get(i) after insertion? The method is void, but we can refer to this.get(...). Use \old for pre-state. The old size is \old(this.size()) or \old(this.getCount())? Here size() method returns size. So use \old(this.size()).

We need to assert: (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i))) );

But need to handle possible nulls; use == null for null checks, and .equals for non-null. Use appropriate parentheses.

Java spec: this.get(i+1) may be null, can't call equals on null. So we need to write condition with null checks.

Thus:

assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i+1) != null && this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) );

But also need to consider case where old element null and new element not null? The spec says either both null, or new equals old. So if old null, new must be null. That's covered.

Thus final assert statement.

Make sure to use parentheses around the implication: assert (0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size())) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); ( (this.get(i+1) == null && \old(this.get(i)) == null) || (this.get(i+1) != null && this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)))) );

Return final code block.

